# The mist engine (@tik-choco/mistlib) and JS wrapper (@tik-choco/mistlib-web)
# come from npm — no configuration or Rust toolchain needed for a normal build.

# --- Working on the engine itself? ---
# Point this at a local `wasm-pack build --target web --release` output (the
# mistlib-wasm/pkg directory of your mistlib-dev checkout) and vite.config.ts
# aliases @tik-choco/mistlib to it — package.json and the lockfile stay clean,
# so there is nothing to revert afterwards. Relative to this app's root.
# Note this redirects Vite only (dev/build/vitest); `tsc` still reads types
# from node_modules. If the engine's API itself changed, install it instead:
#   npm i "@tik-choco/mistlib@file:../mistlib-dev/mistlib-wasm/pkg"
# MISTLIB_LOCAL=../mistlib-dev/mistlib-wasm/pkg
